Matt Frisch <matuse73@yahoo.spam.me.not.com> wrote:
>I don't know whether or not stoning prevents a death drop, but if it does,
>then it is a powerful incentive to not stone.

Only if you're in the habit of stoning things that you couldn't
reasonably defeat by less drastic means.  Compared to one's continued
and comfortable survival, the counterincentive of the lost death-drop
is line noise.

And you do, indeed, lose the death drop if you stone the target.  Calls
to xkilled() made with stoned or (dest & 2) non-zero will not leave a
corpse; neither will deaths for which corpse generation is suppressed by
the character of the level on which the death occurs.  Finally, only
*your* kills via xkilled() leave death drops; victims of pets and
conflict do not leave death drops.
